# Code owners for Juridical.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the listed owner on any PR touching a matching
# path; the LAST matching pattern wins. A ruleset ("Require review from Code
# Owners") makes it an enforced gate. The whole tree defaults to the
# maintainer, with the security-load-bearing surfaces listed explicitly.

*                           @ranklancer

# --- Authorization / audit core (as it lands, per the internal design spec) -----------------
/internal/blast/            @ranklancer
/internal/approve/          @ranklancer
/internal/gate/             @ranklancer
/internal/audit/            @ranklancer
/internal/action/           @ranklancer
/internal/api/              @ranklancer
/internal/source/           @ranklancer
/cmd/juridical/             @ranklancer

# --- Build, release & CI/CD plumbing ---------------------------------------
/.github/                   @ranklancer
/Makefile                   @ranklancer
/.goreleaser.yaml           @ranklancer

# --- Security policy & scanning config -------------------------------------
/SECURITY.md                @ranklancer
/.gitleaks.toml             @ranklancer
/.gitleaksignore            @ranklancer
/.pre-commit-config.yaml    @ranklancer
/tools/pii_scan.sh          @ranklancer

# --- Dependency manifests ---------------------------------------------------
/go.mod                     @ranklancer
/go.sum                     @ranklancer
